    {
      "step": 2,
      "course_id": "EDX1697",
      "rationale": "Build on existing knowledge by introducing the importance of emotional intelligence, cultural sensitivity, and effective communication in conflict resolution. This course helps learners understand their values, strengths, and weaknesses and apply strategic language to craft their personal brand."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "course_id": "EDX1631",
      "rationale": "Foster intrinsic motivation by applying real-world examples and case studies to develop emotional intelligence. This course helps learners build their emotional vocabulary, understand emotional intelligence, and know how to build their emotional intelligence."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "course_id": "EDX840",
      "rationale": "Gradually increase cognitive load by introducing advanced conflict resolution techniques, such as empathy and emotional intelligence. This course helps learners discover the psychological and biological roots of empathy, trust, and cooperation and develop research-based strategies for strengthening empathy and resolving conflicts constructively."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "course_id": "EDX673",
      "rationale": "Pace learning to allow for reflection and application of new skills by introducing effective communication strategies to manage high-conflict situations. This course helps learners outline the relationship between personality disorders and high-conflict personalities and describe some characteristics of narcissistic personality disorder, borderline personality disorder, and antisocial personality disorder."
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "course_id": "EDX2103",
      "rationale": "Foster intrinsic motivation by applying real-world examples and case studies to develop leadership skills. This course helps learners understand how history has shaped expectations of leaders and leadership, factors that contribute to leader emergence and effectiveness, and the role and influence of emotions in leadership."
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "course_id": "EDX3252",
      "rationale": "Gradually increase cognitive load by introducing advanced leadership skills, such as strategic change management. This course helps learners create strategies for change, design initiatives that are impactful and sustainable throughout an organization, and motivate for and implement change in a business while overcoming stakeholder resistance."
    },
    {
      "step": 8,
      "course_id": "EDX3402",
      "rationale": "Pace learning to allow for reflection and application of new skills by introducing inclusive leadership behaviors that make you a more successful leader. This course helps learners understand how to support flexible work environments and better work-life integration, identify barriers to work-life effectiveness, and create solutions."
    },
    {
      "step": 9,
      "course_id": "EDX3406",
      "rationale": "Foster intrinsic motivation by applying real-world examples and case studies to develop inclusive leadership skills. This course helps learners understand behavioral science insights that allow you to create a more inclusive organization, identify DEI issues in the workplace, and implement practical interventions to improve inclusiveness."
    },
    {
      "step": 10,
      "course_id": "EDX3400",
      "rationale": "Gradually increase cognitive load by introducing advanced leadership skills, such as women's leadership program. This course helps learners develop practical tools and strategies to improve their impact and lead others more effectively, understand their unique leadership style, strengths, and limiting behaviors, and strengthen and build their network within their context."
    }
  ]
}

